content.text:
Yes: [srazzak/zed-mdx#21](https://github.com/srazzak/zed-mdx/issues/21), "mdx-analyzer cannot load TypeScript 7 (native) as tsdk", open since 2026-07-19 with no comments and no fix. (The MDX support in Zed is a community extension, not in `zed-industries/zed` — the closest thing there is [zed#60618](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/60618), the same TS 7 breakage for the TypeScript server.)

I confirmed it's your exact cause locally:

- `~/Library/Application Support/Zed/extensions/work/mdx/package.json` pins `"typescript": "7.0.2"`.
- TypeScript 7 is the native Go rewrite. Its `lib/` contains only `getExePath.js`, `tsc.js`, `version.cjs` — no `typescript.js`, no `tsserverlibrary.js`. The Volar-based server loads the tsdk before it reads `typescript.enabled`, so it fails at initialize regardless of settings.
- Extension is at 0.4.0 (latest; last commit 2026-05-10), so there's nothing to upgrade to.

Workaround from the issue: point the tsdk at a TypeScript 5.x lib. This repo has `typescript ^5.8.2` at `node_modules/typescript/lib`, which works:

```json
"lsp": {
  "mdx-analyzer": {
    "initialization_options": {
      "typescript": { "tsdk": "/Users/marklevison/Documents/GitHub/APR/agile-pain-relief-astro/node_modules/typescript/lib" }
    }
  }
}
```

Since that's an absolute repo path, it belongs in this project's `.zed/settings.json` rather than your global Zed settings, or you'd break MDX in other projects. Want me to add it?

Sources: [srazzak/zed-mdx#21](https://github.com/srazzak/zed-mdx/issues/21), [zed-industries/zed#60618](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/60618), [srazzak/zed-mdx](https://github.com/srazzak/zed-mdx)

